 "result": "It's all done by the module-level function `_default` in `src/tessel/json/provider.py:108`. `StandardJSONProvider` (L124) sets it as its `default` attribute (L138). `dumps()` passes it to `json.dumps(default=...)`, so it only runs for objects the standard `json` module can't serialize.\n\n- **Dates:** any `date`, which includes `datetime`, becomes `http_date(o)`, an RFC 822 / HTTP-date string.\n- **UUIDs:** `uuid.UUID` becomes `str(o)`. `decimal.Decimal` gets the same treatment.\n- **Dataclasses:** `dataclasses.is_dataclass(o)` objects become `dataclasses.asdict(o)`, a dict that is then serialized normally.\n- **Other types:** objects with `__html__` (such as `Markup`) become `str(o.__html__())`, and anything else raises `TypeError`.\n\nMy earlier answer called the default provider `DefaultJSONProvider`, which was wrong. The class in this repo is `StandardJSONProvider`. The `response()` behavior I described is correct.",
